"The patient, aged 69 with a PSA of 8.7 and a clinical T-stage of cT1c, was analyzed using the Cox model to predict recurrence time. The model estimates a recurrence window of 14.9 months, and no recurrence event was observed during the follow-up period. This prediction reflects the baseline risk associated with the patient's clinical staging and PSA level, though individual biological variability remains a limitation of prognostic modeling."